Apache-2.0. DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.

The device is SYLforge's: the stationary-lifetime construction of #7616 and #7620 (a register drops a middle stop
while a partner inserts one, the dropped work rides a loan through a carrier, and stationary owned snapshots carry
the rest). #7620 is SYLforge's composition of the 167-CLEAR stationary primal/dual bypasses on #7616 (candidate work
with Claude Opus 5.5 and Antigravity, validation with OpenAI assistance) and builds on Ali Romman's #7605, our #7611
stay drops, Clear1nsight's #7612 contact rechart, Hao Yan/FanPUYen's #7604, SYLforge's #7603, ToikY's #7546/#7544
and Rohan Arun's signed #7113 caller. The base word is our #7621 (courier + helper re-stop on #7620), which builds
on our #7615 and #7617 (courier lineage; #7617 supplies the control word) and on the crowd's courier pattern
(Clear1nsight's #7244/#7274/#7314/#7334/#7481, rohanarun's #7480 and #7277, CubeJerry's #7577, petalas's #7326).

Vendored data (unmodified, data only): data/base-7621-word.json.gz and data/invoice-7621.json are our #7621's
data/word.json.gz and data/invoice-new.json; data/affected-pairs-7620.json is the 837-pair census pinned in #7620's
native runner; engine/data/word-7620.json.gz is #7620's word and engine/data/word-7617.json.gz is #7617's word
(controls only); engine/data/7113_CALLER.json is Rohan Arun's signed #7113 caller (used to price kappa).

engine/ is our own code except three helpers written earlier in this project and vendored with only their path lines
changed: pricekit.py (the exact pricer), fastx.py (randomised-exact replay) and jl.py (kappa under the #7113
caller). No other author's code was run; their words are read as data. check.py adapts the replay, census,
crossing and column-test sections of our #7621 package; its column tests are written from the description of
the affected-pair tests in #7620's README and native runner (512 forward and 512 adjoint Gaussian columns, signed
Pauli action, absolute phase, wrong-phase rejection), following the repository's frozen interpreter and compiler
documented in main.
